          "text": "On admission she was febrile at 37.8°C with a respiratory rate of 28 and oxygen saturations of 84% on home O2; arterial blood gas confirmed type 2 respiratory failure (pH 7.30, PaCO2 8.1). She was commenced on controlled O2 and NIV, and treated with nebulisers, IV hydrocortisone transitioning to oral prednisolone, and IV then oral amoxicillin per local guidelines. She was successfully weaned off NIV by day 3, with saturations returning to her baseline of 88–90% on home O2. Inhaler technique was reviewed, a rescue pack was supplied, and smoking cessation was discussed (she is an ex-smoker).",
